{
  "about": "The memory tool's changes to one target's entries (`entries`, in order) with a size limit (`limit`, characters of the entries joined by \"\\n§\\n\"): one change or a list (`ops`, each `action` add/replace/remove with `content` — or `new_text` — and `old_text`), applied together or not at all; the limit is checked on the result only, and a change that does not grow the entries always goes through. An entry is one fact, at most 400 characters; `old_text` finds an exact entry first, else the one entry containing it. `ok`, the entries after, `message`, `usage`, and `shown` — whether the entries as they were are shown with a refusal, so the model can consolidate. LLeMbas: services/library/memories.py apply_ops; CLI: memory/store.ts applyOps.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "target": "user",
      "entries": [],
      "limit": 1375,
      "ops": [
        {
          "action": "add",
          "content": "Prefers tea."
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "entries": [
          "Prefers tea."
        ],
        "message": "Entry added.",
        "usage": "0% — 12/1,375 chars",
        "shown": false
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "user",
      "entries": [
        "Prefers tea.",
        "Works in Rust and Python.",
        "Lives in Trenčín."
      ],
      "limit": 1375,
      "ops": [
        {
          "action": "add",
          "content": "  Prefers tea.  "
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "entries": [
          "Prefers tea.",
          "Works in Rust and Python.",
          "Lives in Trenčín."
        ],
        "message": "That entry already exists; nothing added.",
        "usage": "4% — 60/1,375 chars",
        "shown": false
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "memory",
      "entries": [
        "Prefers tea.",
        "Works in Rust and Python.",
        "Lives in Trenčín."
      ],
      "limit": 2200,
      "ops": [
        {
          "action": "add",
          "new_text": "Uses Debian."
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "entries": [
          "Prefers tea.",
          "Works in Rust and Python.",
          "Lives in Trenčín.",
          "Uses Debian."
        ],
        "message": "Entry added.",
        "usage": "3% — 75/2,200 chars",
        "shown": false
      }
    },
